      "authority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13",
      "adoption": "Historical incidents for non-China companies may proceed when contained and remediated; current unresolved issues remain held.",
      "usefulness": "Browser Use Cloud billing and session reads provide cheap authenticated inventory without billed session creation.",
      "incident": "24 March 2026 attackers published malicious litellm 1.82.7/1.82.8 on PyPI. Browser Use CLI install.sh depended on litellm>=1.82.2, so CLI installs in that window received credential-harvesting malware. This is an open-source CLI supply-chain incident, not a documented compromise of api.browser-use.com customer API keys. CVE-2025-47241 (URL parsing in the OSS library before 0.1.45) was patched.",
      "remediation": "PyPI removed the malicious litellm versions. Browser Use removed litellm from core dependencies (April\u2013May 2026) and published cleanup guidance. CVE-2025-47241 was fixed in 0.1.45.",
      "residualRisk": "Historical CLI-install supply-chain residual for users who installed during the window and did not rotate credentials. Live Cloud API authentication unverified.",
